@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Windows ACL diagnostic-order correction — 2026-10-29
+
+The second user-run Windows x64 native gate reached the ACL negative tests and
+reported 3 passed, 1 failed, 3 skipped. The failure was an over-specific test
+expectation: `icacls` created an unauthorized Users ACE with `(OI)(CI)(RX)`;
+Cognitum correctly rejected it as `UNEXPECTED_ACE_ACCESS_MASK`, before reaching
+the SID check expected by the test.
+
+This checkpoint reorders *existing mandatory ACL validations*:
+1. ACE type and inheritance flags (unchanged).
+2. Authorization/uniqueness of SID (now before the mask).
+3. Exact full-control access mask (still mandatory for allowed SIDs).
+
+It adds a Windows-only negative test that replaces the *authorized user's*
+full-control ACE with an RX ACE; the auditor must reject it for a wrong mask.
+The earlier unauthorized-Users tests remain unchanged.
+
+Nothing is being allowed that the older auditor rejected. Exact ACE count,
+protected DACL, explicit ACE flags, exact mask, and current-user + SYSTEM
+requirements all remain fail-closed. This is not a Windows pass; rerun natively.
+
+The Windows Python 3.14.6 discovery repair and isolated test runner are preserved.
+Do not modify Lu, AppData or original Cognitum baselines.